{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"32b5e76f-41e3-45ab-83cb-4bff53704f82","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have started running `./run.sh fizz codex 1` to inspect the baseline Codex run behavior and will wait for it to finish.\nWaiting for `./run.sh fizz codex 1` to complete.\nI have initiated a test run of Codex under `sandbox-exec` to observe its behavior and will wait for it to complete.\nWaiting for the background test run of Codex under `sandbox-exec` to complete.\nI have launched a test to verify the sandbox behavior when `-o` points to the run folder, and will wait for it to complete.\nWaiting for the test task to complete.\nI have started the smoke run of `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` and will wait for it to complete.\nWaiting for `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` to complete.\nI have implemented the `codex-sandboxed` lane in [`run.sh`](file:///tmp/h-C8tWoT/run.sh) and documented the work and analysis in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-C8tWoT/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n1. **Added `codex-sandboxed` lane to [`run.sh`](file:///tmp/h-C8tWoT/run.sh)**:\n   - Sets up an isolated scratch home (`/tmp/chome-XXXXXX`) exported as `HOME` and executes Codex via `sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\"`, matching the sandbox boundary used by the Kimi lane.\n   - Copies `auth.json` into the scratch home directory (`$SH/.codex/auth.json`) so Codex can authenticate while sandboxed from the real user home.\n   - Uses a temporary scratch directory in `/tmp` for `-o \"$SCRATCH/final.txt\"` and copies `final.txt` into the target run directory `$R/final.txt` after `sandbox-exec` returns.\n   - Preserves standard stream redirections (`\u003e \"$R/agent.log\" 2\u003e \"$R/agent.err\"`), cleans up scratch folders, and returns the exit code.\n   - Added `codex-sandboxed` to the lane selector `case` statement and header usage comments.\n\n2. **Created [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-C8tWoT/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Detailed what was changed.\n   - Listed